# Run MI against the local mock so failures can be triggered:
#   CUSTOMER_BACKEND_URL=http://customer-mock:3000 docker compose up -d mi
@base = http://localhost:8290

### Backend answers 500 (expect 502 CUSTOMER_BACKEND_ERROR)
GET {{base}}/customers/500

### Backend too slow: mock sleeps 15s, endpoint timeout is 5s (expect 504 CUSTOMER_BACKEND_TIMEOUT after ~5s)
GET {{base}}/customers/999

### Unknown customer (expect 404 CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND)
GET {{base}}/customers/4242

### Backend down (expect 503 CUSTOMER_BACKEND_UNAVAILABLE)
# docker compose stop customer-mock   (then: docker compose start customer-mock)
GET {{base}}/customers/1
